# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even on a Windows checkout. Git's autocrlf
# rewrites them to CRLF, `git archive` ships exactly what is in the working tree,
# and `#!/bin/sh` with a trailing carriage return fails on Linux as
# `set: Illegal option -` — an error that names neither the file nor the reason.
# This deployment ships from a Windows machine to a Linux box every time.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by tools inside the Linux container.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
